# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRIVACY: real citizen data. These must NEVER be committed.
#   context/  insured-property registry (source A), disaster-victim registry
#             (source B: names and ID numbers), field inspection reports
#   outputs/  normalization results derived from the above
# A commit that adds either one leaks personal data irreversibly, because git
# history keeps it even after a later delete.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
context/
outputs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary artifacts: ignored by default, with an explicit whitelist.
#   artifacts/          415 MB (training tensors, evaluation parquets, logs)
#   deploy/artifacts/   199 MB curated serving copy (a copy, always ignored)
# Git cannot re-include a file inside an ignored directory, so the directory
# contents are ignored (`artifacts/*`) and only the model and its config are
# re-included below.
# catastro_emb.pt alone is 161 MB, above GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard limit, so
# committing it is not merely inadvisable, it is rejected. It is regenerable
# (see docs/model-artifacts.md). Recreate the curated copy locally with
# `python deploy/prepare_artifacts.py` before every build or `railway up`
# (see README_DEPLOY.md).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
artifacts/*
!artifacts/model.pt
!artifacts/tuning.json
!artifacts/reliability.json
!artifacts/reliability_v2.json
!artifacts/catastro_meta.json
# catastro_docs.parquet: public cadastre (addresses, parcel ids, centroids), 21 MB.
!artifacts/catastro_docs.parquet
# catastro_own_centroids.parquet: the same public cadastre (NPN + parcel centroid), built by
# scripts/build_own_centroids.py and shipped in the image.
!artifacts/catastro_own_centroids.parquet

# Experiments, row-level evaluations and any run output are never tracked.
artifacts/experiments/

deploy/artifacts/

# Never tracked, whatever the directory: raw evaluation rows contain real
# addresses, tensors and embeddings are large and regenerable.
artifacts/splits/
strict_eval_*
eval_*.csv
eval_*.parquet
*leaderboard*
idesc_*
*predictions*
train_data*
*eval_rows*
*.npz
*.npy
catastro_emb.pt

# Large and not needed to serve.
direcciones_ANN.ipynb
.atl/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

.venv/
venv/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Notebooks are never committed (large, may embed private outputs).
*.ipynb

# Lazily built caches: regenerated on first use (see deploy/prepare_artifacts.py), never commit.
*.pkl
*.joblib
interp_index_v1.*
catalog_keys_v1.*

# Private inputs, run results and scratch.
runs/
candidatos/
salida_jev*/
notebooks/
scratch/
backup/
*.log
.coverage.*
.env*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
